# ============================================================================
# AGB BLACKLIST - Suricata alert rules (agent-side)
# ============================================================================
# Explicit alert rules for known-bad IPs/domains. Every alert here shares
# the "AGB BLACKLIST:" signature prefix, which manager rule 100316 (local
# Docker manager) / 100802 (intern-vm) matches regardless of IP/domain -
# this file IS the single source of truth for C2 IOC enforcement now
# (see local_rules_c2.xml header, 2026-07-03 simplification). Even if
# eve.json shipping to the manager ever breaks, these still alert locally
# in fast.log/eve.json.
#
# IMPORTANT - domain rules (event_type:dns) are alert-only by design, NEVER
# auto-kill: the AR script (agb-kill-block.ps1) detects event_type=dns and
# skips IP-blocking, because dest_ip on a DNS alert is the DNS RESOLVER's
# IP, not the malicious domain's actual IP. Blocking it would firewall your
# own DNS server. If the client then connects to the resolved IP, THAT is
# a separate flow/alert event with the real IP, correctly caught (and
# auto-killed) by the IP-based rules above.
#
# Add one alert rule per known-bad IP or domain. sid range 1000100+
# reserved for this file (do not overlap 1000010+ used in agb-white.rules).
# ============================================================================

# Test C2 used during detection-engineering sessions (2026-06-30/07-01/07-02)
alert ip any any -> 152.42.235.124 any (msg:"AGB BLACKLIST: known test C2 IP 152.42.235.124"; sid:1000100; rev:1;)

# Tor .onion hidden-service DNS queries - generic, not one specific domain.
# Raw .onion resolution attempts are themselves a strong C2/exfiltration
# indicator in most enterprise environments (legitimate business rarely
# needs direct .onion access) - added 2026-07-03. Suffix-anchored regex
# (not a plain content match) so it only matches queries actually ENDING
# in .onion, not domains that merely contain the substring "onion".
alert dns any any -> any any (msg:"AGB BLACKLIST: Tor .onion domain query"; dns.query; pcre:"/\.onion$/i"; sid:1000102; rev:1;)

# Add future known-bad IPs/domains below.
# Example (commented out):
# alert dns any any -> any any (msg:"AGB BLACKLIST: example bad domain"; dns.query; content:"evil.example"; sid:1000103; rev:1;)
